@startuml Memento Pattern - Commission Plan Versioning

' Define the styles (matching observer pattern style)
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam classFontStyle bold
skinparam classBackgroundColor #f8f9fa
skinparam classBorderColor #dee2e6
skinparam arrowColor #6c757d
skinparam stereotypeCBackgroundColor #e9ecef

' Title
title Memento Pattern - Commission Plan Versioning

' Memento
class CommissionPlanMemento <<Memento>> {
  -planId: String
  -planName: String
  -status: PlanStatus
  -effectiveDate: LocalDate
  -expiryDate: LocalDate
  -rules: List<CommissionRule>
  -tiers: List<CommissionTier>
  -bonusRules: List<BonusRule>
  -timestamp: LocalDateTime
  -label: String
  -createdBy: String
  +getTimestamp(): LocalDateTime
  +getLabel(): String
  +getCreatedBy(): String
  +toString(): String
}

' Originator
class CommissionPlanEditor <<Originator>> {
  -plan: CommissionPlan
  -isDirty: boolean
  -editorUsername: String
  +save(label: String): CommissionPlanMemento
  +restore(memento: CommissionPlanMemento): void
  +setPlanName(name: String): void
  +setStatus(status: PlanStatus): void
  +setEffectiveDate(date: LocalDate): void
  +addRule(rule: CommissionRule): void
  +removeRule(rule: CommissionRule): void
  +addTier(tier: CommissionTier): void
  +addBonusRule(bonus: BonusRule): void
  +getPlan(): CommissionPlan
  +isDirty(): boolean
  +display(): void
}

' Caretaker
class VersionHistoryManager <<Caretaker>> {
  -editor: CommissionPlanEditor
  -history: List<CommissionPlanMemento>
  -currentIndex: int
  -maxHistorySize: int
  +checkpoint(label: String): void
  +undo(): boolean
  +redo(): boolean
  +restoreVersion(index: int): boolean
  +restoreCheckpoint(label: String): boolean
  +showHistory(): void
  +compareVersions(index1: int, index2: int): void
  +getCurrentIndex(): int
  +getHistorySize(): int
  +canUndo(): boolean
  +canRedo(): boolean
}

' Domain Model
class CommissionPlan <<DomainModel>> {
  -id: String
  -planName: String
  -status: PlanStatus
  -effectiveDate: LocalDate
  -expiryDate: LocalDate
  -rules: List<CommissionRule>
  -tiers: List<CommissionTier>
  -bonusRules: List<BonusRule>
}

class CommissionRule <<DomainModel>> {
  -ruleName: String
  -commissionRate: BigDecimal
}

class CommissionTier <<DomainModel>> {
  -tierLevel: int
  -minThreshold: BigDecimal
  -maxThreshold: BigDecimal
}

class BonusRule <<DomainModel>> {
  -bonusName: String
  -bonusAmount: BigDecimal
}

enum PlanStatus <<Enumeration>> {
  DRAFT
  ACTIVE
  ARCHIVED
}

' Bonus: Transaction Manager
class DealTransactionManager <<TransactionManager>> {
  -deal: Deal
  -snapshot: Deal
  +beginTransaction(): void
  +commit(): void
  +rollback(): void
  +setTitle(title: String): void
  +setValue(value: BigDecimal): void
  +setStatus(status: DealStatus): void
  +display(): void
}

class Deal <<DomainModel>> {
  -id: String
  -title: String
  -value: BigDecimal
  -status: DealStatus
  -salesRepId: String
  -closeDate: LocalDate
}

' Relationships
CommissionPlanEditor ..> CommissionPlanMemento : creates >
CommissionPlanEditor ..> CommissionPlanMemento : restores from >
CommissionPlanEditor o--> "1" CommissionPlan : edits

VersionHistoryManager o--> "1" CommissionPlanEditor : manages
VersionHistoryManager o--> "0..*" CommissionPlanMemento : stores

CommissionPlanMemento ..> CommissionPlan : captures state of >
CommissionPlanMemento ..> CommissionRule : stores
CommissionPlanMemento ..> CommissionTier : stores
CommissionPlanMemento ..> BonusRule : stores

CommissionPlan --> PlanStatus
CommissionPlan *--> "0..*" CommissionRule
CommissionPlan *--> "0..*" CommissionTier
CommissionPlan *--> "0..*" BonusRule

DealTransactionManager o--> "1" Deal : manages
DealTransactionManager o--> "0..1" Deal : snapshot

' Pattern component notes
note top of CommissionPlanMemento
  <b>Memento</b>

  Stores internal state of CommissionPlan:
  • Immutable snapshot (final fields)
  • Deep copy of all mutable collections
  • Metadata: timestamp, label, creator

  <b>Key principle:</b>
  Only originator (CommissionPlanEditor)
  should access internal state.

  <b>Encapsulation:</b>
  Package-private getters protect state
  from external modification.
end note

note left of CommissionPlanEditor
  <b>Originator</b>

  Creates and restores mementos:
  • save() - creates memento snapshot
  • restore() - restores from memento
  • Editing operations mark as dirty

  <b>Key responsibility:</b>
  Only originator knows how to
  create and interpret mementos.

  <b>State management:</b>
  Tracks isDirty flag to indicate
  unsaved changes.
end note

note right of VersionHistoryManager
  <b>Caretaker</b>

  Manages memento collection:
  • Stores history of mementos
  • Provides undo/redo navigation
  • Enforces history size limits
  • Never examines memento contents

  <b>Features:</b>
  • checkpoint() - save current state
  • undo() - go back one version
  • redo() - go forward one version
  • restoreCheckpoint() - jump to label
  • compareVersions() - diff analysis

  <b>History Management:</b>
  Maintains currentIndex pointer for
  undo/redo stack navigation.
end note

note bottom of CommissionPlan
  <b>Domain Model</b>

  Business object being edited.
  Originator manages this object
  and creates mementos from it.

  Contains complex state:
  • Multiple collections
  • Nested objects
  • Business rules
end note

note bottom of DealTransactionManager
  <b>Transaction Manager</b>

  Simplified memento usage for
  transactional editing:
  • beginTransaction() - save snapshot
  • commit() - keep changes
  • rollback() - restore snapshot

  <b>Use case:</b>
  All-or-nothing editing semantics.
end note

' Interaction flow diagram
note as N1
  <b>TYPICAL INTERACTION FLOW</b>

  <b>1. Checkpoint (Save):</b>
     User → VersionHistoryManager.checkpoint("label")
       → CommissionPlanEditor.save("label")
       → Create CommissionPlanMemento
       → Store in history

  <b>2. Undo:</b>
     User → VersionHistoryManager.undo()
       → Get previous memento from history
       → CommissionPlanEditor.restore(memento)
       → Plan state restored

  <b>3. Redo:</b>
     User → VersionHistoryManager.redo()
       → Get next memento from history
       → CommissionPlanEditor.restore(memento)
       → Plan state restored

  <b>4. Jump to Checkpoint:</b>
     User → VersionHistoryManager.restoreCheckpoint("label")
       → Find memento by label
       → CommissionPlanEditor.restore(memento)
       → Plan state restored

  <b>Key Points:</b>
  • Caretaker never examines memento contents
  • Only originator creates/reads mementos
  • Encapsulation fully preserved
  • Complete undo/redo capability
end note

' Use case diagram
note as N2
  <b>MEMENTO PATTERN USE CASES</b>

  <b>1. Undo/Redo Operations:</b>
     • Navigate through edit history
     • Restore previous states
     • Re-apply undone changes

  <b>2. Named Checkpoints:</b>
     • Mark important milestones
     • Jump to specific versions
     • Compare different versions

  <b>3. Draft Editing:</b>
     • Experiment with changes
     • Discard if unsuccessful
     • Restore published version

  <b>4. Version Comparison:</b>
     • Diff two versions
     • See what changed
     • Audit trail analysis

  <b>5. Transactional Editing:</b>
     • Begin/commit/rollback
     • All-or-nothing semantics
     • Safe complex operations

  <b>6. Auto-Save/Recovery:</b>
     • Periodic snapshots
     • Crash recovery
     • No data loss
end note

' Legend
legend right
  <b>Memento Pattern Components:</b>

  <b>Memento:</b> Stores internal state snapshot
  of originator. Immutable and opaque to
  caretaker. Only originator can access state.

  <b>Originator:</b> Creates mementos containing
  snapshots of its internal state. Uses
  mementos to restore previous state.

  <b>Caretaker:</b> Responsible for memento
  safekeeping. Never operates on or examines
  memento contents. Manages history and
  provides undo/redo functionality.

  <b>Key Benefits:</b>
  ✓ Preserves encapsulation
  ✓ Simplifies originator (no history mgmt)
  ✓ Powerful undo/redo capability
  ✓ Version history and checkpoints
  ✓ Transactional operations
  ✓ Safe experimentation

  <b>Encapsulation Principle:</b>
  Caretaker stores mementos but never
  examines them. Only originator knows
  how to create and interpret mementos.

  <b>Memory Consideration:</b>
  Mementos can consume significant memory.
  Implement history limits, compression,
  or incremental snapshots for optimization.
endlegend

' State flow visualization
note as N3
  <b>STATE HISTORY VISUALIZATION</b>

  History Stack (currentIndex = 2):
  ┌─────────────────────────────────┐
  │ 0. Initial Draft                │
  ├─────────────────────────────────┤
  │ 1. Added Rules                  │
  ├─────────────────────────────────┤
  │ 2. Activated ← CURRENT          │
  ├─────────────────────────────────┤
  │ 3. Added Bonuses                │
  └─────────────────────────────────┘

  <b>Operations:</b>
  • undo() → currentIndex--
  • redo() → currentIndex++
  • checkpoint() → add at currentIndex+1,
                   clear forward history
  • restoreVersion(n) → currentIndex = n

  <b>History Pruning:</b>
  When new checkpoint created at index < last,
  all forward history is discarded.
  Example: checkpoint at index 2 removes index 3.
end note

@enduml